            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The contents of a cell can be duplicated in consecutive cells."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The duplication factor and operator are applied to a "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "cell’s specifier"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "add-cells-and-rows.html#specifiers"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and allow you to clone a cell’s content and properties across consecutive cells. A duplication is the first operator in a cell specifier."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "duplication factor"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "strong",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "><"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "duplication operator"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "strong",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "><horizontal alignment operator><vertical alignment operator><style operator>|<cell’s content>"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "example",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "duplication factor"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is a single integer ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<n>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") that indicates how many times the cell’s content should be duplicated."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "duplication operator"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is an asterisk ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "*"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") placed directly after the duplication factor ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<n>*"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). The duplication operator tells the converter to interpret the duplication factor as part of a duplication instead of a span."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "_duplication_factor_and_operator",
        "level": 1,
